.TH SDL_GetThreadName 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetThreadName \- Get the thread name as it was specified in
.BR SDL_CreateThread ().

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_thread.h>
.PP
.BI "const char * SDL_GetThreadName(SDL_Thread *thread);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I thread
the thread to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to a UTF-8 string that names the specified thread, or NULL if it doesn\(aqt have a name\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

